        <profile name="Emanatus Force Field (Aura)" id="d111-fa6a-81a4-d278" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">Against ranged attacks, friendly ADEPTUS MECHANICUS BATTLELINE models wholly within 6" of this model have a 4+ invulnerable save.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Scuttling Walker" id="0922-f382-6d65-c703" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When the unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move:
  -&gt; The triggering unit can move over friendly Monster models as though they were not there.
  -&gt; The triggering unit can move over friendly Vehicle models as though they were not there.
  -&gt; The triggering unit can move over terrain features 4" or lower as though they were not there.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Deadly Demise" id="b763-5345-cda7-92ed" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When this model is destroyed, after the units embarked within it have made their emergency disembark moves:
  -&gt; Roll one D6: on a 6+, for each unit: while the unit is within 6" of this model, the unit suffers a number of mortal wounds equal to its rating.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Damaged" id="fa6d-7851-4382-8265" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">While the model has X or fewer wounds remaining, X being its rating, this model gets -1 to Hit rolls.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
